{"name":"Sea Turtle","hex":"#818a40","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea turtle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any turtle that inhabits oceans, especially of the superfamily Chelonioidea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_turtle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea turtle","blocks":[{"text":"Sea turtles, sometimes called marine turtles, are reptiles of the order Testudines and of the suborder Cryptodira. The seven existing species of sea turtles are the flatback, green, hawksbill, leatherback, loggerhead, Kemp's ridley, and olive ridley. Five of the seven species are listed as threatened with extinction globally on the IUCN Red List of Threatened Species. The remaining two are not considered to be threatened with extinction, one of which, the flatback turtle, is found only in the waters of Australia, Papua New Guinea, and Indonesia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Chelonia_mydas_is_going_for_the_air_edit.jpg/330px-Chelonia_mydas_is_going_for_the_air_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_turtle"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"},{"title":"Turtle","blocks":[{"text":"Turtles are reptiles characterized by a special shell developed mainly from their ribs. Modern turtles are divided into two major groups, the Pleurodira and Cryptodira, which differ in the way the head retracts. There are 360 living and recently extinct species of turtles, including land-dwelling tortoises and freshwater terrapins. They are found on most continents, some islands and, in the case of sea turtles, much of the ocean. Like other amniotes they breathe air and do not lay eggs underwater, although many species live in or around water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Turtle_diversity.jpg/330px-Turtle_diversity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Nature_La_R%C3%A9union%2C_janvier_2018_47.jpg/500px-Nature_La_R%C3%A9union%2C_janvier_2018_47.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Nature_La_R%C3%A9union%2C_janvier_2018_47.jpg/1280px-Nature_La_R%C3%A9union%2C_janvier_2018_47.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Nature_La_R%C3%A9union%2C_janvier_2018_47.jpg/500px-Nature_La_R%C3%A9union%2C_janvier_2018_47.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Green (left) and loggerhead (right) sea turtles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANature_La_R%C3%A9union%2C_janvier_2018_47.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Protostega_gigas.jpg/500px-Protostega_gigas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Protostega_gigas.jpg/1280px-Protostega_gigas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Protostega_gigas.jpg/500px-Protostega_gigas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_